# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Input. Modes 5 and 6 (`ozirchunk`): the input of mode 2 (compiler/emit_wasm.a0 `wairchunk`),
# then the eval program (function count, 7 words each; node count, 6 words each; operand
# count, pairs) and its map (one word per chunk function: eval index + 1, 0 when absent).
# Mode 4 (`ozsunit`): the input of mode 1, then the eval program as source (byte count,
# bytes: formatted functions, parsed by the A0 front end and not checked) and its map (word
# count, then the words).

fn ozirchunk io bool -> (io,u32)
r1 call wardw p0
base at r1 0
t1 at r1 1
r2 call wardw t1
from at r2 0
t2 at r2 1
nd mul from 2
rd call warn16 t2 nd
dt at rd 0
t3 at rd 1
r4 call wardw t3
nty at r4 0
