r8 call wardw t7
nf at r8 0
t8 at r8 1
nfw mul nf 7
rf call warn45 t8 nfw
fs at rf 0
t9 at rf 1
r10 call wardw t9
nn at r10 0
t10 at r10 1
nnw mul nn 6
rn call warn128 t10 nnw
nds at rn 0
t11 at rn 1
ry call warn24 t11 nn
nty2 at ry 0
t12 at ry 1
r13 call wardw t12
no at r13 0
t13 at r13 1
now mul no 2
ra call warn512 t13 now
ar at ra 0
t14 at ra 1
r15 call wardw t14
npl at r15 0
t15 at r15 1
rp call warn400 t15 npl
pl at rp 0
t16 at rp 1
nfm mul nf 2
rm call warn16 t16 nfm
fm at rm 0
t17 at rm 1
e1 call wardw t17
nef at e1 0
t18 at e1 1
nefw mul nef 7
ef call warn45 t18 nefw
efn at ef 0
t19 at ef 1
e2 call wardw t19
nen at e2 0
t20 at e2 1
nenw mul nen 6
en call warn128 t20 nenw
enode at en 0
t21 at en 1
e3 call wardw t21
nea at e3 0
t22 at e3 1
neaw mul nea 2
ea call warn512 t22 neaw
earg at ea 0
t23 at ea 1
em call warn16 t23 nf
emap at em 0
t24 at em 1
z8 call z8
w call ozemit t24 ty tl fs nds ar nty2 pl fm dt z8 nty from nf base no efn enode earg emap p1
ret w
end
# mode 4: `wasunit` (compiler/emit_wasm.a0) with the optimizer. Lex, parse and check the
# source p1 of p2 bytes, functions [p4, nfns) given the iteration bounds p3; parse the eval
# program source p7 (p8 bytes; not checked); with no diagnostic, optimize the chunk (call table
# p5, p6 variants before it) with the eval program and its map p9, and emit it. (io code)
fn ozsunit io u32x512x64 u32 u32x128x8 u32 u32x128x16 u32 u32x512x64 u32 u32x128x16 -> (io,u32)
lx call lexsrc p1 p2
